# Files excluded from the Vercel build container. These are pipeline inputs
# and local-only assets that `next build` never reads - excluding them cuts
# ~185 MB from every build's input (including the dozens of daily deployments
# that only run the ignore step).
Overture-Per-Country-Raw/
Overture-Match-Suggestions/

# Secrets and local debris, excluded 2026-09-23. None of these is read by
# `next build`, and each is a thing that should never reach a deployment even
# by accident.
#
# .env*            every env file. .env.example is tracked and harmless, but
#                  the pattern is the point: a .env.local dropped in the repo
#                  root must not be uploaded to the build container.
# betatestkeys.txt not tracked today. Listed so that if it ever is added by
#                  hand it is excluded from the moment it appears, rather than
#                  after someone notices.
# *.bak*           THREE OF THESE ARE TRACKED AND WERE BEING DEPLOYED:
#                  public/data/leaders/_defunct.json.bak-shangzhou-20260721,
#                  the matching _modern-territory one, and
#                  public/data/uk-commons-history.json.bak-ukcommons-20260721,
#                  about 400 KB of editing debris served as static files.
#                  Checked before excluding: nothing READS a .bak path at
#                  build or run time. Several one-off scripts WRITE *.bak
#                  backups beside a file they edit, but those run locally and
#                  never inside the build container.
.env*
betatestkeys.txt
*.bak*
